$ enola install --help
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola install [flags] [repo_path]

Write enola's instructions into the files your coding agents read.

By default this writes INSTRUCTIONS ONLY — inert context telling the agent the
tools exist. Pass --hooks to also run the loop automatically: a baseline pinned
at session start, and the architectural delta reported at the end if the change
introduced a regression. Hooks run commands, so they are opt-in.

Flags:
  -dry-run
    	show what would change, write nothing
  -global
    	configure this user (all projects) instead of this repository
  -hooks
    	also install the session-start and stop hooks (install only)
  -targets string
    	comma-separated subset of: claude, cursor, agents, codex, copilot, pi, opencode
  -yes
    	skip the confirmation prompt

Examples:
  # Tell your agents enola is here (instructions only)
  enola install

  # ...and close the loop automatically with session hooks
  enola install --hooks

  # Preview what that would change, writing nothing
  enola install --hooks --dry-run

  # For every project of this user, two agents only
  enola install --global --targets=claude,cursor

See also: enola help uninstall, enola help doctor
